-- title:
--   q-expansion field of X_H(M) generated by j(qᵖ)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number, let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and assume $p \mid M$, $p^2 \nmid M$, and that $H$ contains the kernel of the reduction homomorphism $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, i.e. every unit $u$ of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ with `ZMod.unitsMap` image $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ lies in $H$. Work inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$, realised as `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`. For a level $N$ and subgroup $H'$, `xHFunctionFieldBar N H'` denotes `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (xHFunctionField N H')`, that is the intermediate field generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise image under `coeffEmb` of the rational $q$-expansion field `xHFunctionFieldC ℚ N H'` attached to $(N,H')$. The assertion is that the join, in the lattice of intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, of `xHFunctionFieldBar (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` — level $M/p$ with the image `H.map (ZMod.unitsMap …)` of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ — and of the field generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the single Laurent series `qExpand (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) p (jqModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`, obtained from the $j$-series $q^{-1}\,(E_4^3\eta^{-24})$ by the substitution $q \mapsto q^p$ on exponents, equals `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`.
--
--   This is the classical statement that for $p$ exactly dividing $M$ and $H$ the full preimage of its image $H'$ modulo $M/p$, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-function field of $X_H(M)$ is generated over that of $X_{H'}(M/p)$ by $j(q^p)$, the two fields differing in degree $p+1$. It is used in the analysis of places and specialisations of the $J_H$-tower, and in identifying automorphisms of $X_H(M)$ that act trivially on the subfield coming from `infSubgroup`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_xHFunctionFieldBar_div_sup_adjoin_qExpand_jqModC_eq_xHFunctionFieldBar.lean

